ed output format: tab-separated, header 'Sample\\tCluster', Sample_1 through Sample_90, integer cluster labels (0, 1, 2). (5) The only warning was a benign joblib/loky message about lscpu not being found, which does not affect results. Confidence score: 100% — the code ran cleanly, the algorithm matches the specification, and the output file is correctly formatted with 90 samples assigned to 3 balanced clusters (30/30/30). No modification is required. Code data and results: Both input CSVs loaded successfully (90 samples each, no missing values, all float64). The SNF fusion produced a 90×90 fused similarity matrix. Spectral clustering yielded perfectly balanced clusters (Cluster 0: 30, Cluster 1: 30, Cluster 2: 30), which is plausible for simulated/standardized data. Output file saved to /mnt/data/lengyang/youjia_project/autoba/BABench/src/promptbio-bench/tasks/b-5-10/result_79/toolsgenie_20260709/data/snf_cluster_assignments.txt in tab-separated text format with header 'Sample\\tCluster'. No multiple plan steps were executed inadvertently — this is a single SNF + clustering step. Next actions for Supervisor Agent: Proceed to the next step. The SNF integration and spectral clustering task is complete with valid output generated.\n", "<class 'langchain_core.messages.ai.AIMessage'>: The SNF analysis has been completed successfully. Here's the updated plan checklist:\n\n**Step 1.** [✓] Inspect input data files — 90 samples × 99 genes (expression) and 90 samples × 29 genes (CNV), both standardized, no missing values\n**Step 2.** [✓] Implement SNF: construct Euclidean distance → scaled Gaussian affinity matrices (K=20 neighbors) for each view, iteratively fuse (T=20 iterations) into a single 90×90 fused similarity matrix\n**Step 3.** [✓] Apply spectral clustering with 3 clusters on the fused matrix (normalized Laplacian → 3 smallest eigenvectors → KMeans) and output `snf_cluster_assignments.txt`\n\n### Summary of Results\n\n| Step | Detail |\n|------|--------|\n| **Input** | Gene expression (90×99) + CNV (90×29), both standardized |\n| **Affinity matrices** | Scaled Gaussian kernel with K=20 nearest neighbors per view |\n| **Fusion** | 20 iterations of SNF cross-diffusion (Q₁·P₂·Q₁ᵀ and Q₂·P₁·Q₂ᵀ) |\n| **Clustering** | Spectral clustering: normalized Laplacian → 3 eigenvectors → KMeans (k=3, random_state=42) |\n| **Cluster sizes** | Cluster 0: 30, Cluster 1: 30, Cluster 2: 30 (perfectly balanced) |\n\n**Output file**: `snf_cluster_assignments.txt` — tab-separated with header `Sample\\tCluster`, containing 90 rows (Sample_1 through Sample_90) with integer cluster assignments (0, 1, 2). The file is saved at:\n`/mnt/data/lengyang/youjia_project/autoba/BABench/src/promptbio-bench/tasks/b-5-10/result_79/toolsgenie_20260709/data/snf_cluster_assignments.txt`\n\nThe perfectly balanced clusters (30/30/30) are consistent with the standardized nature of the input data and suggest three distinct subgroups of tumor samples were successfully identified through multi-view integration."], 'input_token_num': 32995, 'output_token_num': 9592}
